# Generated key material for the example stacks — never committed.
#
# This lives at examples/ level, not inside each example, so it protects every
# example regardless of which one exists on a given branch. A per-example
# .gitignore does not help when a sibling directory is created first: a broad
# `git add examples` then sweeps up that sibling's generated secrets before its
# own .gitignore is in the tree, which is exactly how a .env got committed once.
**/.env
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.crt
**/*.csr
**/*.srl
